<title>USA: Delaware State Housing, $43 mln bond deal repriced.</title>
<headline>Delaware State Housing, $43 mln bond deal repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney said Tuesday that it repriced Delaware State Housing Authority $43 million bond deal, lowering yields in five basis points in the 2026 and 2028 maturities.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>DELAWARE STATE HOUSING AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $43,065,000*</p>
<p>SENIOR SINGLE FAMILY MORTGAGE REVENUE BONDS,</p>
<p>1997 SERIES A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE PRICE CHANGES IN 2026 AND 2028.</p>
<p>ALL ORDERS WILL BE CONSIDERED GOOD IN THOSE MATURIIES UNLESS</p>
<p>WE HEAR FROM YOU BY 1:00 PM TODAY.</p>
<p>WE EXPECT TO HAVE BALANCES IN THE FOLLOWING MATURITIES:  1998, 1999, 2001, 2003, 2008 THROUGH 2010.</p>
<p>			     SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>		 (A1 under.conf)</p>
<p>AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 03/15/1997	    FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01 &amp; 01/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR. MATURITY		AMOUNT*   AMOUNT*   COUPON</p>
<p>			   (1/1)    (7/1)</p>
<p>1998		     150M	 --     3.70  %</p>
<p>1998			--	 115M    3.85  %</p>
<p>1999		     405M	 --     4.10  %</p>
<p>1999			--	 400M    4.25  %</p>
<p>2000		     400M	410M    4.45  %</p>
<p>2001		     420M	430M    4.60  %</p>
<p>2002		     440M	450M    4.75  %</p>
<p>2003		     460M	470M    4.85  %</p>
<p>2004		     485M	495M    4.95  %</p>
<p>2005		     510M	520M    5.10  %</p>
<p>2006		     535M	550M    5.20  %</p>
<p>2007		     560M	575M    5.30  %</p>
